# RESERVED-NAME-BINDINGS (Codex K03-RESERVED-NAME-ANSWER-20261006-02/-03; dictionary :128, CORE :648, grammar §5):
# a word of the language cannot name a binding of the program -- refused at the name by the one admission
# (l2_bind_admit), in either spelling, whether or not the word has a lowering yet.
# Here: a local of a nested body named break, refused at the name.
fn: m () int
    if: 1 = 1
        int: break 3
    ---
    return: 7
end: m
sendMessage: exit(exit_code: m(); stdout: ""; stderr: "")
return
